<title>ITALY: Italy's Perugia sees Sept CPI at 4.1 pct yr/yr.</title>
<headline>Italy's Perugia sees Sept CPI at 4.1 pct yr/yr.</headline>
<dateline>PERUGIA, Italy 1996-09-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Italian city of Perugia said its September consumer price index stood at 0.9 percent month-on-month and 4.1 percent year-on-year.</p>
<p>In August, Perugia's inflation rate was 0.1 percent and 3.5 percent respectively.</p>
<p>Perugia is one of 10 Italian cities publishing inflation data on Monday and Tuesday.</p>
<p>The city's CPI has a weighting of 1.26 percent on the national index. The 10 sample cities have a combined weighting of 69.67 percent on the total index.  </p>
<p>Following is the breakdown of the price changes.</p>
<p>(figures in brackets refer to August 1996):</p>
<p>					    Month/Month     Year/Year</p>
<p>    General index		     0.9   (0.1)     4.1  (3.5)</p>
<p>    Food				  0.5   (0.2)     4.7  (4.9)</p>
<p>    Clothing and footwear	   0.4   (0.0)     4.7  (4.4)</p>
<p>    Housing and utility charges   0.6   (0.6)     4.9  (4.3)</p>
<p>    Furniture			  -0.2   (0.1)     2.9  (3.2)</p>
<p>    Health services		   0.2   (0.0)     2.4  (2.3)</p>
<p>    Transportation		    0.0   (0.3)     3.9  (4.1)</p>
<p>    Entertainment and culture     8.0   (0.0)     9.2  (1.3)</p>
<p>    Education			   0.0   (0.2)     4.7  (4.8)</p>
<p>    Hotels and restaurants	  0.3   (0.0)     2.5  (2.8)</p>
<p>    Other goods or services	 0.2  (-0.3)     1.8  (1.8)</p>
<p>-- Milan newsroom +392 66129526</p>
